# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Omarchy Mobile storage guard, continued in Arch. The initramfs marks every UFS
# partition read-only except userdata, and removes the whole-disk node of the
# main LUN. udev would recreate the whole-disk nodes, so make them
# inaccessible and keep desktop tools from touching any Android partition.
# The Saga's UFS has eight LUNs (sda to sdh). sda is the main LUN; sde holds
# slot A's boot partitions, and a later initramfs leaves sde writable at the
# disk level (its ro flag 0) so that three of them can be updated through
# their own partition nodes. Its whole-disk node would then reach every
# partition on the LUN, so it gets the same treatment as sda. Mode 0000
# keeps users and desktop tools off a node; root can still open it, and
# the ro flags stay the guard.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sda|sde", MODE="0000", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="sd[a-z][0-9]*", ENV{ID_PART_ENTRY_NAME}!="userdata", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
